173
01:06:36,880 --> 01:06:39,880
Yeah, almost nobody, right.

174
01:06:39,880 --> 01:06:42,840
So, yes, I mean, I looked at the general survey.

175
01:06:42,840 --> 01:06:46,640
So, out of people who only studied a foreign language

176
01:06:46,640 --> 01:06:51,920
in school, under 1% claim that they can speak the foreign

177
01:06:51,920 --> 01:06:54,240
language very well, right.

178
01:06:54,240 --> 01:06:56,280
Now, how many jobs are available to people

179
01:06:56,280 --> 01:06:58,880
who can half speak a foreign language?

180
01:06:58,880 --> 01:07:01,240
Yeah, very few.

181
01:07:01,240 --> 01:07:03,360
Maybe high school Spanish teacher, actually.

182
01:07:03,360 --> 01:07:07,080
You've seen King of the Hill, but even that,

183
01:07:07,080 --> 01:07:08,960
that's a little unclear.

184
01:07:08,960 --> 01:07:11,320
But, you know, and there's the obvious point of, look,

185
01:07:11,320 --> 01:07:13,360
thanks to immigration, there are tons of people

186
01:07:13,360 --> 01:07:15,080
who are totally fluent in the foreign language.

187
01:07:15,080 --> 01:07:19,360
You don't need to go and get a native made crummy imitation.

188
01:07:19,360 --> 01:07:23,320
So, there's like no real point of studying a foreign language

189
01:07:23,320 --> 01:07:27,160
for most people, but you need it to get into a good college.

190
01:07:27,160 --> 01:07:29,160
And then, and if you don't get the college degree,

191
01:07:29,160 --> 01:07:31,160
then you need it for a good job.

192
01:07:31,160 --> 01:07:33,320
So, you have to go and do this thing when you're a teenager

193
01:07:33,320 --> 01:07:35,280
that has no apparent effect on your productivity

194
01:07:35,280 --> 01:07:37,200
in almost any job you're going to do.

195
01:07:37,200 --> 01:07:40,760
And yet, if you don't do it, you are really hurting yourself.

196
01:07:40,760 --> 01:07:44,720
Yeah, so in my book, I point out I could not be a professor

197
01:07:44,720 --> 01:07:47,480
in this office if I had just said foreign language is stupid.

198
01:07:47,480 --> 01:07:48,800
You don't need it in America.

199
01:07:48,800 --> 01:07:50,320
Instead, I went and did three years

200
01:07:50,320 --> 01:07:53,880
of god awful foreign language instruction, which was both,

201
01:07:53,880 --> 01:07:56,240
failed to teach me the language, but also filled me

202
01:07:56,240 --> 01:07:59,760
with great anxiety about Spanish.

203
01:07:59,760 --> 01:08:01,920
Because, like, what they did to me.

204
01:08:01,920 --> 01:08:04,160
It was horrible.

205
01:08:04,160 --> 01:08:07,040
Once a month, you had to memorize a speech in Spanish

206
01:08:07,040 --> 01:08:09,240
and deliver it without any notes.

207
01:08:09,240 --> 01:08:12,160
Because that's a great way to learn a foreign language, right?

208
01:08:12,160 --> 01:08:14,800
Is to give a memorized five-minute speech

209
01:08:14,800 --> 01:08:15,600
in a foreign language.

210
01:08:15,600 --> 01:08:17,920
That's how you really learn to speak, right?

211
01:08:17,920 --> 01:08:19,800
Whereas, we never actually spoke to each other

212
01:08:19,800 --> 01:08:21,600
in the foreign language in class.

213
01:08:21,600 --> 01:08:23,960
Anyway, so I still get really freaked

214
01:08:23,960 --> 01:08:26,720
out when I remember these horrible times.

215
01:08:26,720 --> 01:08:27,760
I have them like nine times.

216
01:08:27,760 --> 01:08:29,360
And then, on the last one, the teacher,

217
01:08:29,360 --> 01:08:30,760
the teacher said it wasn't for a grade.

218
01:08:30,760 --> 01:08:33,960
And so, and then I did a really bad job.

219
01:08:33,960 --> 01:08:35,360
And then, she said, well, in that case,

220
01:08:35,360 --> 01:08:37,840
I'm going to drop you a full grade in the class.

221
01:08:37,840 --> 01:08:40,520
Like, you didn't say that was a possible effect.

222
01:08:40,520 --> 01:08:43,880
In fact, I specifically asked, what if you do a terrible job?

223
01:08:43,880 --> 01:08:45,560
And the effect, no, as long as you get up there.

224
01:08:45,560 --> 01:08:47,960
And then, after everyone else had gone,

225
01:08:47,960 --> 01:08:51,560
then she did the sub game imperfect thing of saying, no,

226
01:08:51,560 --> 01:08:54,000
I'm not really going to drop your grade.

227
01:08:54,000 --> 01:08:58,040
Anyway, that one, like, compounded the PTSD from that.

228
01:08:58,040 --> 01:09:01,400
Perhaps I'm more vulnerable to this than I am.

229
01:09:01,400 --> 01:09:02,360
All right.

230
01:09:02,360 --> 01:09:04,640
Anyway, and then, if you start making lists of other classes

231
01:09:04,640 --> 01:09:08,920
that you must take to advance along the educational pyramid,

232
01:09:08,920 --> 01:09:10,320
even though you are almost certain

233
01:09:10,320 --> 01:09:12,440
to never use it in real life.

