01:17:32,880 --> 01:17:35,840
Or will he have devised a theory that explains each

444
01:17:35,840 --> 01:17:36,960
and every case?

445
01:17:36,960 --> 01:17:39,080
Right? And of course, the answer is, we've got a theory

446
01:17:39,080 --> 01:17:40,680
to explain each and every case.

447
01:17:40,680 --> 01:17:43,280
So at least a popular way to resolve all

448
01:17:43,280 --> 01:17:45,560
of these seemingly paradoxical results,

449
01:17:45,560 --> 01:17:48,280
those are the name of signaling.

450
01:17:48,280 --> 01:17:50,160
There's lots of signaling models,

451
01:17:50,160 --> 01:17:53,200
but they've all got three basic assumptions.

452
01:17:53,200 --> 01:17:54,520
First of all, there's the assumption

453
01:17:54,520 --> 01:17:57,640
that there are different types of people, firms, animals,

454
01:17:57,640 --> 01:17:58,800
things.

455
01:17:58,800 --> 01:18:01,680
All right, so the types might be able versus unable,

456
01:18:01,680 --> 01:18:03,840
smart versus dumb, honest and dishonest,

457
01:18:03,840 --> 01:18:06,960
hardworking and lazy, all sorts of possible types

458
01:18:06,960 --> 01:18:08,240
out there in the world.

459
01:18:08,240 --> 01:18:10,200
All right, so that's step one.

460
01:18:10,200 --> 01:18:12,920
All right, step two is that we've

461
01:18:12,920 --> 01:18:14,520
got asymmetric information about type.

462
01:18:14,520 --> 01:18:15,020
Why?

463
01:18:20,080 --> 01:18:24,040
Because you know whether you're hardworking or lazy, probably.

464
01:18:24,040 --> 01:18:26,600
But if you go to interview for a job,

465
01:18:26,600 --> 01:18:29,640
and they ask you, are you A, hardworking, or B, lazy?

466
01:18:29,640 --> 01:18:32,120
What does almost everybody say?

467
01:18:32,120 --> 01:18:32,720
Hardworking.

468
01:18:32,720 --> 01:18:34,880
Everyone's hardworking, which means

469
01:18:34,880 --> 01:18:36,400
that there's asymmetric information,

470
01:18:36,400 --> 01:18:38,600
because you know whether you're hardworking or not.

471
01:18:38,600 --> 01:18:41,360
But as far as employers are concerned, on the surface,

472
01:18:41,360 --> 01:18:43,280
everybody looks the same.

473
01:18:43,280 --> 01:18:45,280
It's a bunch of people all claiming

474
01:18:45,280 --> 01:18:48,560
to be married to their jobs.

475
01:18:48,560 --> 01:18:50,320
So there's that.

476
01:18:50,320 --> 01:18:52,920
Also hard to observe the types correctly.

477
01:18:52,920 --> 01:18:55,880
And then the last assumption, the key one,

478
01:18:55,880 --> 01:18:58,840
is that different types have different costs

479
01:18:58,840 --> 01:19:00,560
of doing something observable.

480
01:19:00,560 --> 01:19:14,320
So there's got to be different costs in observable activity.

481
01:19:14,320 --> 01:19:16,560
And then when you put these three together,

482
01:19:16,560 --> 01:19:19,400
the result is if you are the good type,

483
01:19:19,400 --> 01:19:20,960
then you know that you are not going

484
01:19:20,960 --> 01:19:24,000
to get credit for being good just because you say I'm good.

485
01:19:24,000 --> 01:19:25,700
Instead, what you're going to want to do

486
01:19:25,700 --> 01:19:29,280
is to find something to do that convinces outside observers

487
01:19:29,280 --> 01:19:30,680
that you're good.

488
01:19:30,680 --> 01:19:33,880
You want to do something that would be really

489
01:19:33,880 --> 01:19:36,120
expensive for a bad person to do,

490
01:19:36,120 --> 01:19:38,320
less expensive for a good person to do,

491
01:19:38,320 --> 01:19:42,600
so that it is believable that you actually are good.

492
01:19:42,600 --> 01:19:44,400
That's the whole idea.

493
01:19:44,400 --> 01:19:48,000
Now, if we have something like this,

494
01:19:48,000 --> 01:19:51,360
then it can be in the interest of whoever

495
01:19:51,360 --> 01:19:53,440
is in higher demand, whoever gets better treatment

496
01:19:53,440 --> 01:19:58,640
in the world, to go to school and study Aristotle.

497
01:19:58,640 --> 01:20:01,440
Not because you need to know it.


1
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:02,640
Aristotle to do a good job, not because it has any effect

2
01:20:02,640 --> 01:20:04,240
on your productivity as a worker,

3
01:20:04,240 --> 01:20:06,520
but because you are showing off.

