01:20:14,920 --> 01:20:18,040
but I have completed the college curriculum.

8
01:20:18,040 --> 01:20:21,040
Ta-da, that is a big deal, right?

9
01:20:21,040 --> 01:20:23,040
Whereas being, I'm one class short

10
01:20:23,040 --> 01:20:24,600
of completing the college curriculum,

11
01:20:24,600 --> 01:20:27,600
oh, fire me, not a very good pitch.

12
01:20:27,600 --> 01:20:31,480
All right, so I've completed a college curriculum.

13
01:20:31,480 --> 01:20:34,040
Right, that is a very compelling, right?

14
01:20:34,040 --> 01:20:38,320
And the idea there is that there are good and bad workers,

15
01:20:38,320 --> 01:20:41,080
right, but of course, everyone claims to be good.

16
01:20:41,080 --> 01:20:42,840
But if you are a good worker,

17
01:20:42,840 --> 01:20:46,640
you also probably find it easier in some sense

18
01:20:46,640 --> 01:20:48,760
to do well in school and to finish.

19
01:20:48,760 --> 01:20:49,920
Whereas if you're not so good,

20
01:20:49,920 --> 01:20:52,480
then you probably don't find it so easy, right?

21
01:20:52,480 --> 01:20:54,200
And the idea is there's a lot of overlap

22
01:20:54,200 --> 01:20:56,720
between the work ethic and the school ethic.

23
01:20:56,720 --> 01:20:59,520
Someone who's a good student is normally a good worker.

24
01:20:59,520 --> 01:21:01,200
Doesn't need to always be true, of course.

